{"term":"involve","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:1a59df232aed713641","definition":"To have (something) as a component or a related part; to comprise, to include.","example":"My job involves forecasting economic trends.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["comprehend"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["disinvolve","interinvolve","involved","involvement","involver","no human involved","reinvolve","uninvolve","uninvolving"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/involve#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5abf9b51494507e6ab","definition":"To cause or engage (someone or something) to become connected or implicated, or to participate, in some activity or situation.","example":"By involving herself in her local community, Mary met lots of people and also helped make it a nicer place to live.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["include"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["disinvolve","interinvolve","involved","involvement","involver","no human involved","reinvolve","uninvolve","uninvolving"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/involve#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0ca10b4d66f5335b72","definition":"To entangle, intertwine, or mingle (something with one or more other things, or several things together); especially, to entangle (someone or something) in a confusing or troublesome situation.","example":"to involve a person in debt or misery","pos":"verb","synonyms":["blend","ensnarl","implicate","merge","admix","amalgamate","bemingle","blend","combine","commingle","intermingle","intermix","involve","mang","meddle","ming","mingle","mix","mix up","enmesh","ensnare","ensnarl","entangle","foul","implicate","imply","involve","mat","ravel","snarl","tangle"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, transitive","wordFamily":["disinvolve","interinvolve","involved","involvement","involver","no human involved","reinvolve","uninvolve","uninvolving"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/involve#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2b409f5c8a92f5b03e","definition":"To cover or envelop (something) completely; to hide, to surround.","example":"to involve in darkness or obscurity","pos":"verb","synonyms":["enfold","enwrap","swallow up"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, transitive","wordFamily":["disinvolve","interinvolve","involved","involvement","involver","no human involved","reinvolve","uninvolve","uninvolving"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/involve#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1b1d3cfd77558cfc74","definition":"To form (something) into a coil or spiral, or into folds; to entwine, to fold up, to roll, to wind round.","example":"VVe muſt be ſtiffe and ſteddie in reſolue. / Let's thus our hands, our hearts, our armes inuolue.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, transitive","wordFamily":["disinvolve","interinvolve","involved","involvement","involver","no human involved","reinvolve","uninvolve","uninvolving"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/involve#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:75940965764c9d87fc","definition":"To make (something) intricate; to complicate.","example":"And as wililye as thoſe ſhrewes that beguyle hym haue holpe hym to inuolue and intryke the matter: I ſhall vſe ſo playn and open a way therin, that euery man ſhall well ſee the trouth.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic, obsolete","register":"archaic, obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["disinvolve","interinvolve","involved","involvement","involver","no human involved","reinvolve","uninvolve","uninvolving"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/involve#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e692c6108e8f3309b2","definition":"To multiply (a number) by itself a given number of times; to raise to any assigned power.","example":"a quantity involved to the third or fourth power","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic, obsolete","register":"archaic, obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["disinvolve","interinvolve","involved","involvement","involver","no human involved","reinvolve","uninvolve","uninvolving"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/involve#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ɪnˈvɒlv/"},"wordFamily":["disinvolve","interinvolve","involved","involvement","involver","no human involved","reinvolve","uninvolve","uninvolving"]}